": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/teng-lin", "html_url": "https://github.com/teng-lin", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/teng-lin/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/teng-lin/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/teng-lin/gists{/gist_id}", "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/teng-lin/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/teng-lin/subscriptions", "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/teng-lin/orgs", "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/teng-lin/repos", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/teng-lin/events{/privacy}", "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/teng-lin/received_events", "type": "User", "user_view_type": "public", "site_admin": false}, "jobs_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/teng-lin/open-foresight/actions/runs/39506520356/jobs", "logs_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/teng-lin/open-foresight/actions/runs/39506520356/logs", "check_suite_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/teng-lin/open-foresight/check-suites/107062632267", "artifacts_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/teng-lin/open-foresight/actions/runs/39506520356/artifacts", "cancel_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/teng-lin/open-foresight/actions/runs/39506520356/cancel", "rerun_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/teng-lin/open-foresight/actions/runs/39506520356/rerun", "previous_attempt_url": null, "workflow_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/teng-lin/open-foresight/actions/workflows/388025431", "head_commit": {"id": "02d572fbd66022bb125d188dfa296ba7f2bf85bc", "tree_id": "e8c2f74ae4190273c9bc7cf5d94c9aaabc0d7943", "message": "Treat a listener that closes during a connect as gone, not an error (#162)\n\n* fix: treat a listener that closes during a connect as gone, not an error\n\nThe S2 socket test failed under load: just after the first listener\nclosed, the probe before the next publish found the path in use. The\ntest runner runs suites as isolates of one process, so a child another\nsuite forked while the listener was open holds a copy of it until the\nchild calls exec (the socket is close-on-exec, not close-on-fork). A\nconnect in that window either is accepted, so the probe rightly reports\na live listener, or waits in the backlog until the copy goes and then\nfails with ECONNRESET. Dart reports that second case as a bare OSError\nrather than a SocketException, so it escaped probeSocketPath and broke\npublish, clearStaleSocket and `--stop`; ServiceClient.connect let it\nescape ensureService's startup loop the same way when a closing\nowner's listener went during a connect.\n\nprobeSocketPath now catches the bare OSError and asks again after\nECONNRESET, since the listener that connect reached has closed.\nServiceClient.connect reports the bare OSError as a SocketException.\nThe S2 test waits until nothing accepts at the path before the next\npublish, so a forked child's copy no longer makes it fail. New tests\nforce a connect to wait in the backlog of a listener that then closes.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_013zVTtpJUaD4vQHEarRRjkw\n\n* fix: retry a reset probe once past its bound and keep the connect stack\n\nFrom review of the #161 fix: the first reset is asked again even after\nthe 200 ms bound, since the load that delays reading it does not delay\nthe next connect. Resets and the macOS refused-connect retries now have\nseparate counters. The mapped SocketException keeps the original stack\ntrace, and the connect test pins the reset path (errno 104), so a plain\nrefused socket cannot pass it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_013zVTtpJUaD4vQHEarRRjkw\n\n* fix: treat a reset connect as not forwarded in the desktop\n\nA second desktop launch forwards to the running desktop. If that desktop\nclosed its command listener during the connect, the pending reset came\nback as a bare OSError, escaped AppCommands.forward and showed the\nfailure screen instead of letting the new launch take over. Found in\nreview of the #161 fix.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_013zVTtpJUaD4vQHEarRRjkw\n\n* fix: give a probe retried after a reset a real connect timeout\n\nA retry after a reset may start past the 200 ms bound, and its 1 ms\ntimer could fire before isolate scheduling let the connect complete,\nwhich reads as 'cannot tell' and refuses a socket that is provably\ngone. Retries after a reset now wait at least 50 ms. From CodeRabbit's\nreview of #162.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_013zVTtpJUaD4vQHEarRRjkw\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>", "timestamp": "2026-10-20T22:13:29Z", "author": {"name": "Teng Lin", "email": "teng.lin@gmail.com"}, "committer": {"name": "GitHub", "email": "noreply@github.com"}}, "repository": {"id": 1421509295, "node_id": "R_kgDOVLqCrw", "name": "open-foresight", "full_name": "teng-lin/open-foresight", "private": false, "owner": {"login": "teng-lin", "id": 737447, "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjczNzQ0Nw==", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/737447?v=4", "gravatar_id": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/teng-lin", "html_url": "https://github.com/teng-lin", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/teng-lin/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/teng-lin/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/teng-lin/gists{/gist_id}", "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/teng-lin/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/teng-lin/subscriptions", "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/teng-lin/orgs", "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/teng-lin/repos", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users